<title>USA: Consumers Mich. nuke seen back by Monday.</title>
<headline>Consumers Mich. nuke seen back by Monday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumers Energy's 67 megawatt Big Rock Point nuclear power plant is expected to return to service on Sunday or Monday following a repair outage, a company spokesman said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Big Rock Point, located in Charlevoix, Mich., was shut March 2 to repair a leak.</p>
<p>Consumers is a subisidiary of CMS Energy Corp.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627))</p>
